file session-logs/date/20260906/20260906-180617_the-box-that-read-only-its-own-handwriting.kyri the parked lap's own record, landed with its numbers swept
scope recovering one parked lap of this tree's own, landing it under fetched numbers, folding one closed row off a tight pin, and closing the race its own hot pass surfaced
status GREEN -- reds_citation, stash_record and reds_monotone all green on metal; hot roster run at the close
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- three want your word. **The race**: eight ships share one TMPDIR and nine control pens still name a constant, so one ship can delete another's pen mid-build; the instance that reddened my own send is repaired and proven both ways, the nine are booked by name across five lanes, and until they turn, every ship keeps recording every other ship's races as flakes. **The ledger's silence about work in flight**: this lap withdrew a second row to a peer, and the two of us independently chose the same shelf FILENAME 44 seconds apart -- should an OPEN row carry a claim, a seat and a stamp, at start? That question now has a price and a filename attached. **The card**: it stood at 30 bytes of slack before I wrote a word, and my account went 2,073 to 747 to fit; every ship is over its 2,048 and the pin holds on trimming alone. Also unchanged: 82 of 607 reachable living pages lead nowhere, scored 100 by a ceiling with no floor.
